e landing point for."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A pattern's rationale is that it answers the problem this node states.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r12-two-layer-calibration.flexiarg", :sha256 "49eac90f07daa81f9cd6013137eefb2c2681dcd3927b42e7df09fa39dbc7fd2d"}, :situation-source "Fragment 0-40 '# Mission: Pattern Retrieval Calibration' names the activity; pattern IF 'A pattern's rationale is that it answers the problem this node states.'", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A calibration activity is being named and framed as a mission."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The problem, verbatim from the dossier: Control-stage R12 solves separating internal consistency from externally witnessed value evidence: the roster places **“Two-layer calibration”** in BELIEVE's assurance band (`control-stages.edn:40`; control-stage/catalogue numbering). Catalogue R12 requires Layer 1 and Layer 2 to retain distinct labels, and permits only independently witnessed Layer 2 to clear value (`p4ng/sec-catalog.tex:297`; catalogue R12). Contract R12 instead specifies a slower outer loop that treats inner-loop hyperparameters as hidden state (`docs/futon-aif-completeness.md:286-294`; contract R12, a different node). The equation registry classifies control-stage R12 as plumbing and gives it no equation (`aif-equations.edn:472-473`; control-stage R12). The control-stage problem is therefore provenance-preserving calibration: cheap self-consistency may inform the record but cannot impersonate external value evidence. (source: futon2 holes labs wm-contract PROBLEMS-assurance-band-batch6.md, R12, The problem it solves)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r12-two-layer-calibration.flexiarg", :sha256 "49eac90f07daa81f9cd6013137eefb2c2681dcd3927b42e7df09fa39dbc7fd2d"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER, dossier R12 'provenance-preserving calibration: cheap self-consistency may inform the record but cannot impersonate external value evidence'.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Calibration must separate internal self-consistency from externally witnessed value evidence."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer it; solving the problem itself is scoped by the dossier's residual-problems list, not by this node.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r12-two-layer-calibration.flexiarg", :sha256 "49eac90f07daa81f9cd6013137eefb2c2681dcd3927b42e7df09fa39dbc7fd2d"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE, census L1 'only six problem-stating nodes for 1256 patterns'.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "The mission exists because problem nodes for calibration were otherwise unreachable."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [0], :pattern "problems/r12-two-layer-calibration"} {:pattern-rationale "Calibration exists because pattern relevance lacks a recognised rationale; this sentence states the mission's response.", :fragment-span {:start 54, :end 67}, :occurrence-id ["problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale" 1], :roles ["context" "condition"], :source-sha256 "54a64c1b7b1cdaa632aebe0f86d370c96cf39262c17ae62e0d5db9b860276230", :sentence-id "s2", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale", :objects {:G {:text "    A pattern whose rationale is unrecognised cannot be refused for lacking one, and a cascade built over such patterns cannot be certified at graph grain.\n    + evidence: futon2 holes labs wm-contract EPIC-run-era.md, \"## The theory-track ruling (Joe, 2026-09-05, pre-flight) — the library loop, rationale reachability, graph certificates\".", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale.flexiarg", :sha256 "54a64c1b7b1cdaa632aebe0f86d370c96cf39262c17ae62e0d5db9b860276230"}, :situation-source "Fragment text 'OPEN — DERIVE'; pattern THEN lands @why edges from rationale-annotation work.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Mission status OPEN — DERIVE marks the stage at which rationale reachability is being derived."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A library of patterns feeds cascade construction, and cascades are to carry graph-level certificates.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale.flexiarg", :sha256 "54a64c1b7b1cdaa632aebe0f86d370c96cf39262c17ae62e0d5db9b860276230"}, :situation-source "Fragment 54-67 'OPEN — DERIVE' shows the mission in progress; pattern IF covers the library that feeds cascades.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The mission document is itself an active artefact in the rationale-carrying corpus."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The problem, per the ruling (Joe, verbatim, 2026-09-05): \"the programme here would continue the library loop, mining the evidence landscape and annotating patterns, so that we get a sense of what problems we have been solving historically. even though we only have 20 nodes and a comparable number of WR patterns, we have a whole library of other patterns, and it would be good if this would all come together... Right now most patterns would be unreachable via @how or @why traversal, ie. they have no globally recognised rationale. While this is clearly different from the Lean issues, ultimately we will want graph-level certificates too, and these tracks should eventually merge around on the fly cascade construction and processing\". Measured on the L1 census: 1146 of 1264 committed patterns carry no authored @why and at least 95% are @why-unreachable from any problem-stating node under every reading. (source: futon2 holes labs wm-contract EPIC-run-era.md, The theory-track ruling, 2026-09-05; measurement: futon2 holes labs library-loop runs L1-census-receipt.edn and runs L4-certificate-strawman-receipt.edn)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale.flexiarg", :sha256 "54a64c1b7b1cdaa632aebe0f86d370c96cf39262c17ae62e0d5db9b860276230"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER, L1 census measurement (95% @why-unreachable under every reading).", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Despite open status, the corpus it works over is largely rationale-unreachable."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer rationale-annotation; solving it is the library-loop lane's program (L5-L12), not this node's.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale.flexiarg", :sha256 "54a64c1b7b1cdaa632aebe0f86d370c96cf39262c17ae62e0d5db9b860276230"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE 'a cascade built over such patterns cannot be certified at graph grain'.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Certification at graph grain is impossible while rationale reachability is unmeasured."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [1], :pattern "problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale"} {:pattern-rationale "Calibration exists because pattern relevance lacks a recognised rationale; this sentence states the mission's response.", :fragment-span {:start 127, :end 141}, :occurrence-id ["problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale" 2], :roles ["context"], :source-sha256 "54a64c1b7b1cdaa632aebe0f86d370c96cf39262c17ae62e0d5db9b860276230", :sentence-id "s3", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale", :objects {:G {:text "    A pattern whose rationale is unrecognised cannot be refused for lacking one, and a cascade built over such patterns cannot be certified at graph grain.\n    + evidence: futon2 holes labs wm-contract EPIC-run-era.md, \"## The theory-track ruling (Joe, 2026-09-05, p