quare-v1, :pattern "problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons", :objects {:G {:text "    A section whose documentation states one shared problem carries one problem node, not per-pattern copies (the L11/L15/L18 cost finding).\n\n    + evidence: futon3 library/data-mining/README.md, opening paragraph; the L18 v3 complete search receipt runs/L18-remainder.edn.", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg", :sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0"}, :situation-source "Fragment rationale 'Enforcement is staged: advisory first'; pattern THEN 'per-pattern questions route to the section documentation'.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Advisory mode routes per-pattern questions to documented lessons instead of invention."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Work happens in or consumes the data-mining section's patterns.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg", :sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0"}, :situation-source "Fragment 795-817 'advisory mode first,' staged enforcement.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Advisory-first staging is a pipeline decision over model-over-corpus outputs."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The section's own documentation states the problem: \"Lessons distilled from the futon6 meme-mining (forward: turns -> memes/methods) and goals-and-holes (backward: turns -> C-entries/belly) runs on a rented GPU box, 2026-06-25/26. They generalize to any pipeline that runs a model over a large corpus to extract structured records\" (source: futon3 library/data-mining/README.md, opening paragraph)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg", :sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER quoting data-mining README opening paragraph.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The lessons generalise to any pipeline running a model over a corpus, including this gate's advice."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    This node is the landing point for @why edges from the data-mining worklist members (mechanical pass, row L18 v3); per-pattern questions route to the section documentation, not to invention here.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg", :sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE on one problem node per documented section.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "One shared mining-problem statement carries one node; staging avoids per-pattern copies."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [15], :pattern "problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons"} {:pattern-rationale "The mining cross-ref established the substrate by probing the claimed property rather than a proxy.", :fragment-span {:start 817, :end 864}, :occurrence-id ["pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy" 16], :roles ["condition" "dependency"], :source-sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99", :sentence-id "s15", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy", :objects {:G {:text "    Local success and global trust coincide only when the property is local.\n    A compiler run cannot by itself establish axiom cleanliness, source grep\n    cannot see imported placeholders, and a matching top-level hash cannot see\n    unhashed meaning changes.  Probing the promised property prevents the gate\n    from certifying a different, easier claim.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg", :sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"}, :situation-source "Fragment rationale 'Enforced mode waits until a violation corpus exists'; pattern THEN on direct probes before the gate.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "The gate defers acceptance until the violation corpus (the direct probe) exists."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The acceptance signal checks a representation of the property rather than\n    the property itself, especially when imports, definitions, historical\n    state, or human verdicts contribute to the claim.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg", :sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"}, :situation-source "Fragment 817-864 'enforced mode after a violation corpus exists.'", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Enforced mode's claimed property (violation detection) needs a real corpus, not a proxy signal."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Direct probes can be expensive, and some properties have no complete\n    decision procedure.  A dependency-closure audit may require building\n    previously unbuilt artifacts; a semantic vacuity check remains heuristic.\n    Calling an incomplete probe complete merely creates a new proxy.  State the\n    probe's coverage, retain explicit unknown/skipped outcomes, and reserve\n    acceptance for the portion actually checked.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg", :sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER 'Calling an incomplete probe complete merely creates a new proxy'.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Building a violation corpus is the expensive direct probe; calling advisory mode complete would be a new proxy."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Write the promised property as a checkable question; identify its trust\n    closure; run the strongest available direct probe on every member of that\n    closure; test the probe against known-good, known-bad, and multi-defect\n    fixtures; and make uncovered or skipped members visible non-success states.\n    Keep cheap proxies only as triage filters before this gate.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg", :sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE 'Probing the promised property prevents the gate from certifying a different, easier claim'.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Enforcing without the corpus would certify an easier claim than violation detection."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [16], :pattern "pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy"} {:pattern-rationale "The cross-ref list is the mission reading what exists before acting.", :fragment-span {:start 865, :end 936}, :occurrence-id ["cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first" 17], :roles ["context" "contrast"], :source-sha256 "04b442f40edd33be35382de2355944a0135c50dbefce4a7ec5967378ec21d81e", :sentence-id "s16", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first", :objects {:G {:text "    The disagreements decide which patterns the cascade needs; a cascade built without them restates the requirement.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first.flexiarg", :sha256 "04b442f40edd33be35382de2355944a0135c50dbefce4a7ec5967378ec21d81e"}, :situation-source "Fragment rationale 'Cross-reference to the B→A complement mission'; pattern THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Citing the complement file is the reading-first act on the other side."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A cascade is to be constructed for a problem.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first.flexiarg", :sha256 "04b44