ruction/read-what-exists-first"} {:pattern-rationale "Directly the lessons from mining the pattern corpus that this mission calibrates against.", :fragment-span {:start 158, :end 227}, :occurrence-id ["problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons" 4], :roles ["context" "dependency"], :source-sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0", :sentence-id "s5", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons", :objects {:G {:text "    A section whose documentation states one shared problem carries one problem node, not per-pattern copies (the L11/L15/L18 cost finding).\n\n    + evidence: futon3 library/data-mining/README.md, opening paragraph; the L18 v3 complete search receipt runs/L18-remainder.edn.", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg", :sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0"}, :situation-source "Fragment text; pattern THEN 'per-pattern questions route to the section documentation'.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "The cross-ref routes per-pattern questions to the mining documentation rather than invention here."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Work happens in or consumes the data-mining section's patterns.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg", :sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0"}, :situation-source "Fragment 158-227 cites `holes/missions/M-pattern-mining.md`; pattern IF 'Work happens in or consumes the data-mining section's patterns.'", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "This mission consumes the data-mining section's mining outputs."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The section's own documentation states the problem: \"Lessons distilled from the futon6 meme-mining (forward: turns -> memes/methods) and goals-and-holes (backward: turns -> C-entries/belly) runs on a rented GPU box, 2026-06-25/26. They generalize to any pipeline that runs a model over a large corpus to extract structured records\" (source: futon3 library/data-mining/README.md, opening paragraph)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg", :sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER quoting library/data-mining/README.md opening paragraph.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The mining substrate was produced by running a model over a large corpus, the exact pipeline class the problem generalises to."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    This node is the landing point for @why edges from the data-mining worklist members (mechanical pass, row L18 v3); per-pattern questions route to the section documentation, not to invention here.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons.flexiarg", :sha256 "ee946ca8da244de23cb996b5e318979a7cf6f53ff83e0bb704d817e764f561e0"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE 'A section whose documentation states one shared problem carries one problem node'.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "One shared problem statement carries one node, not per-pattern copies."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [4], :pattern "problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons"} {:pattern-rationale "The mining cross-ref established the substrate by probing the claimed property rather than a proxy.", :fragment-span {:start 228, :end 299}, :occurrence-id ["pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy" 5], :roles ["condition" "rationale"], :source-sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99", :sentence-id "s6", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy", :objects {:G {:text "    Local success and global trust coincide only when the property is local.\n    A compiler run cannot by itself establish axiom cleanliness, source grep\n    cannot see imported placeholders, and a matching top-level hash cannot see\n    unhashed meaning changes.  Probing the promised property prevents the gate\n    from certifying a different, easier claim.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg", :sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"}, :situation-source "Fragment rationale 'The finding: the cosine substrate produces artifacts'; pattern THEN 'run the strongest available direct probe'.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "The artifact-prone finding is the result of probing the claimed property instead of the acceptance proxy."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The acceptance signal checks a representation of the property rather than\n    the property itself, especially when imports, definitions, historical\n    state, or human verdicts contribute to the claim.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg", :sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"}, :situation-source "Fragment 228-299 reports the mining mission's finding; pattern IF 'acceptance signal checks a representation of the property rather than the property itself'.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The substrate's claimed property (similarity as relevance) had been checked only through a representation of it."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Direct probes can be expensive, and some properties have no complete\n    decision procedure.  A dependency-closure audit may require building\n    previously unbuilt artifacts; a semantic vacuity check remains heuristic.\n    Calling an incomplete probe complete merely creates a new proxy.  State the\n    probe's coverage, retain explicit unknown/skipped outcomes, and reserve\n    acceptance for the portion actually checked.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg", :sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER 'Direct probes can be expensive, and some properties have no complete decision procedure'.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Direct probing of embedding relevance is expensive and has no complete decision procedure."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Write the promised property as a checkable question; identify its trust\n    closure; run the strongest available direct probe on every member of that\n    closure; test the probe against known-good, known-bad, and multi-defect\n    fixtures; and make uncovered or skipped members visible non-success states.\n    Keep cheap proxies only as triage filters before this gate.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg", :sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE 'Probing the promised property prevents the gate from certifying a different, easier claim'.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "The gate must not certify a different, easier claim than sensor cleanliness."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [5], :pattern "pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy"} {:pattern-rationale "The MiniLM-cosine channel's precision is exactly what the mission says is untrusted.", :fragment-span {:start 300, :end 320}, :occurrence-id ["problems/r7-evidence-channel-precision" 6], :roles ["condition" "contrast"], :source-sha256 "693a6df8f213f79fadb7dd144b93591ab103ededd319348c7d7f89612543684c", :sentence-id "s7", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "problems/r7-evidence-channel-precision", :objects {:G {:text "    The census (library-loop L1) found only six problem-stating nodes for 1256 patterns, so most @why edges had nothing to land on; minting the dossier problems as nodes is the recorded-corpus repair.\n    + evidence: futon2 holes labs wm-contract PROBLEMS-r2-r8-r7-batch2.md, section \"## R7 — Evidence-channel precision\", subsection \"The problem it solves\".", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r7-evidence-channel-precision.flexiarg", :sha256 "693a6df8f213f79fadb7dd144b93591ab103ededd319348c7d7f89612543684c"}, :situation-source "Fragment relations [condition, contrast]; pattern THEN lands @why edges answering channel precision.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Denying clean-sensor status is the precision demotion this node governs."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A pattern's rationale is that it answers the problem this node states.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r7-evidence-channel-precision.flexiarg", :sha256 "693a6df8f213f79fadb7dd144b93591ab103ededd319348c7d7f89612543684c"}, :situation-source "Fragment 300-320 'as a clean sensor.' names the needed channel.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The mission needs a clean sensor for pattern relevance."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The problem, verbatim from the dossier: R7 solves how the loop varies trust by evidence channel without discarding noisy evidence: the roster places **“Evidence-channel precision”** in BELIEVE (`p4ng/empirics-futon/control-stages.edn:20`; control-stage numbering). The operational criterion says channels with persistent high error lose precision and those with persistent low error gain it, with the update carried across ticks (`docs/futon-aif-completeness.md:175-190`; contract R7). The catalogue requires **“one trust weight per kind of evidence”** applied wherever error, scoring, or gating occurs, so trust remains auditable rather than prompt rhetoric (`p4ng/sec-catalog.tex:200`; catalogue R7). The registry defines the update as `Pi_k := 1 / max(Var(eps_k), eps0)` and records that variance is taken over the bounded history of channel-k prediction errors (`holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:81-84`; control-stage R7). Here capital `Pi` means evidence-channel precision (inverse error variance): it is neither policy carrier `pi` nor policy precision `gamma = 1/beta`, the three-way symbol hazard recorded at `holes/labs/wm-contract/EPIC-run-era.md:719-721`. (source: futon2 holes labs wm-contract PROBLEMS-r2-r8-r7-batch2.md, R7, The problem it solves)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r7-evidence-channel-precision.flexiarg", :sha256 "693a6df8f213f79fadb7dd144b93591ab103ededd319348c7d7f89612543684c"}, :situation-source "Fragment rationale 'The denied claim'; pattern HOWEVER operational criterion on persistent error.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The MiniLM-cosine channel's persistent error means it cannot be granted precision, but its evidence is not discarded."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer it; solving the problem itself is scoped by the dossier's residual-problems list, not by this node.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r7-evidence-channel-precision.flexiarg", :sha256 "693a6df8f213f79fadb7dd144b93591ab103ededd319348c7d7f89612543684c"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER citing catalogue R7 and the Pi_k variance update.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "The demotion must be recorded as an auditable per-channel trust weight."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [6], :pattern "problems/r7-evidence-channel-precision"} {:pattern-rationale "The mining cross-ref established the substrate by probing the claimed property rather than a proxy.", :fragment-span {:start 455, :end 524}, :occurrence-id ["pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy" 9], :roles ["condition" "goal"], :source-sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99", :sentence-id "s10", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy", :objects {:G {:text "    Local success and global trust coincide only when the property is local.\n    A compiler run cannot by itself establish axiom cleanliness, source grep\n    cannot see imported placeholders, and a matching top-level hash cannot see\n    unhashed meaning changes.  Probing the promised property prevents the gate\n    from certifying a different, easier claim.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg", :sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"}, :situation-source "Fragment rationale 'Quality bar for pattern application'; pattern THEN 'Write the promised property as a checkable question'.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Each bar term is to be written as a checkable question with a direct probe."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The acceptance signal checks a representation of the property rather than\n    the property itself, especially when imports, definitions, historical\n    state, or human verdicts contribute to the claim.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg", :sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"}, :situation-source "Fragment 455-524 states the bar; pattern IF on acceptance signals checking representations.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The application bar ('well-specified, repeatable, demonstrably useful') could be satisfied by proxies."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Direct probes can be expensive, and some properties have no complete\n    decision procedure.  A dependency-closure audit may require building\n    previously unbuilt artifacts; a semantic vacuity check remains heuristic.\n    Calling an incomplete probe complete merely creates a new proxy.  State the\n    probe's coverage, retain explicit unknown/skipped outcomes, and reserve\n    acceptance for the portion actually checked.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg", :sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER on incomplete probes and explicit unknown/skipped outcomes.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Demonstrable usefulness of pattern application has no complete decision procedure; a probe's coverage must be stated."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Write the promised property as a checkable question; identify its trust\n    closure; run the strongest available direct probe on every member of that\n    closure; test the probe against known-good, known-bad, and multi-defect\n    fixtures; and make uncovered or skipped members visible non-success states.\n    Keep cheap proxies only as triage filters before this gate.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg", :sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE on local success and global trust coinciding only when the property is local.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Usefulness certified by proxy would certify an easier claim than the one promised."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [9], :pattern "pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy"} {:pattern-rationale "The cross-ref list is the mission reading what exists before acting.", :fragment-span {:start 525, :end 595}, :occurrence-id ["cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first" 10], :roles ["context"], :source-sha256 "04b442f40edd33be35382de2355944a0135c50dbefce4a7ec5967378ec21d81e", :sentence-id "s11", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first", :objects {:G {:text "    The disagreements decide which patterns the cascade needs; a cascade built without them restates the requirement.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first.flexiarg", :sha256 "04b442f40edd33be35382de2355944a0135c50dbefce4a7ec5967378ec21d81e"}, :situation-source "Fragment text; pattern THEN 'Read the four sources first and record where they disagree'.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Citing the excursion file is the act of reading what exists first."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A cascade is to be constructed for a problem.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first.flexiarg", :sha256 "04b442f40edd33be35382de2355944a0135c50dbefce4a7ec5967378ec21d81e"}, :situation-source "Fragment 525-595 cites `holes/excursions/E-pattern-peripheral.md`.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A companion excursion exists and must be read before acting."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Reading takes time, and a plausible cascade can be written from the problem statement in minutes.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first.flexiarg", :sha256 "04b442f40edd33be35382de2355944a0135c50dbefce4a7ec5967378ec21d81e"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER 'a plausible cascade can be written from the problem statement in minutes'.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The companion could be summarised from the mission statement alone in minutes."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Read the four sources first and record where they disagree.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first.flexiarg", :sha256 "04b442f40edd33be35382de2355944a0135c50dbefce4a7ec5967378ec21d81e"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE 'The disagreements decide which patterns the cascade needs'.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Disagreement between creation-side and retrieval-side gates decides the mission's shape."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [10], :pattern "cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first"} {:pattern-rationale "Calibration exists because pattern relevance lacks a recognised rationale; this sentence states the mission's response.", :fragment-span {:start 596, :end 661}, :occurrence-id ["problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale" 11], :roles ["contrast" "context"], :source-sha256 "54a64c1b7b1cdaa632aebe0f86d370c96cf39262c17ae62e0d5db9b860276230", :sentence-id "s12", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale", :objects {:G {:text "    A pattern whose rationale is unrecognised cannot be refused for lacking one, and a cascade built over such patterns cannot be certified at graph grain.\n    + evidence: futon2 holes labs wm-contract EPIC-run-era.md, \"## The theory-track ruling (Joe, 2026-09-05, pre-flight) — the library loop, rationale reachability, graph certificates\".", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale.flexiarg", :sha256 "54a64c1b7b1cdaa632aebe0f86d370c96cf39262c17ae62e0d5db9b860276230"}, :situation-source "Fragment rationale 'The excursion gates the creation side, symmetric to this retrieval side'; pattern THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Symmetry with the creation side is how the retrieval side earns graph-level certificates."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A library of patterns feeds cascade construction, and cascades are to carry graph-level certificates.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale.flexiarg", :sha256 "54a64c1b7b1cdaa632aebe0f86d370c96cf39262c17ae62e0d5db9b860276230"}, :situation-source "Fragment 596-661 'the symmetric *creation*-side gate'; pattern IF on the library feeding cascade construction.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The creation-side gate is itself part of the pattern library's certified-cascade programme."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The problem, per the ruling (Joe, verbatim, 2026-09-05): \"the programme here would continue the library loop, mining the evidence landscape and annotating patterns, so that we get a sense of what problems we have been solving historically. even though we only have 20 nodes and a comparable number of WR patterns, we have a whole library of other patterns, and it would be good if this would all come together... Right now most patterns would be unreachable via @how or @why traversal, ie. they have no globally recognised rationale. While this is clearly different from the Lean issues, ultimately we will want graph-level certificates too, and these tracks should eventually merge around on the fly cascade construction and processing\". Measured on the L1 census: 1146 of 1264 committed patterns carry no authored @why and at least 95% are @why-unreachable from any problem-stating node under every reading. (source: futon2 holes labs wm-contract EPIC-run-era.md, The theory-track ruling, 2026-09-05; measurement: futon2 holes labs library-loop runs L1-census-receipt.edn and runs L4-certificate-strawman-receipt.edn)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale.flexiarg", :sha256 "54a64c1b7b1cdaa632aebe0f86d370c96cf39262c17ae62e0d5db9b860276230"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER, L1 census 95% @why-unreachable.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Both sides of the gate currently sit in a corpus where most patterns lack recognised rationale."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer rationale-annotation; solving it is the library-loop lane's program (L5-L12), not this node's.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale.flexiarg", :sha256 "54a64c1b7b1cdaa632aebe0f86d370c96cf39262c17ae62e0d5db9b860276230"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE 'a cascade built over such patterns cannot be certified at graph grain'.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Graph-grain certification is unavailable until rationale reachability improves on both sides."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [11], :pattern "problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale"} {:pattern-rationale "Names calibration as a two-layer problem, matching this mission's framing of retrieval-side calibration against the mining findings.", :fragment-span {:start 662, :end 693}, :occurrence-id ["problems/r12-two-layer-calibration" 12], :roles ["goal" "contrast"], :source-sha256 "49eac90f07daa81f9cd6013137eefb2c2681dcd3927b42e7df09fa39dbc7fd2d", :sentence-id "s13", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "problems/r12-two-layer-calibration", :objects {:G {:text "    The census (library-loop L1) found only six problem-stating nodes for 1256 patterns, so most @why edges had nothing to land on; minting the dossier problems as nodes is the recorded-corpus repair.\n    + evidence: futon2 holes labs wm-contract PROBLEMS-assurance-band-batch6.md, section \"## R12 — Two-layer calibration\", subsection \"The problem it solves\".", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r12-two-layer-calibration.flexiarg", :sha256 "49eac90f07daa81f9cd6013137eefb2c2681dcd3927b42e7df09fa39dbc7fd2d"}, :situation-source "Fragment rationale 'This mission is the retrieval-side half of the gate'; pattern THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "The retrieval-side half is this mission's landing point for two-layer calibration."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A pattern's rationale is that it answers the problem this node states.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r12-two-layer-calibration.flexiarg", :sha256 "49eac90f07daa81f9cd6013137eefb2c2681dcd3927b42e7df09fa39dbc7fd2d"}, :situation-source "Fragment 662-693 '*retrieval*-side calibration.'", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A retrieval-side calibration activity is being scoped."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The problem, verbatim from the dossier: Control-stage R12 solves separating internal consistency from externally witnessed value evidence: the roster places **“Two-layer calibration”** in BELIEVE's assurance band (`control-stages.edn:40`; control-stage/catalogue numbering). Catalogue R12 requires Layer 1 and Layer 2 to retain distinct labels, and permits only independently witnessed Layer 2 to clear value (`p4ng/sec-catalog.tex:297`; catalogue R12). Contract R12 instead specifies a slower outer loop that treats inner-loop hyperparameters as hidden state (`docs/futon-aif-completeness.md:286-294`; contract R12, a different node). The equation registry classifies control-stage R12 as plumbing and gives it no equation (`aif-equations.edn:472-473`; control-stage R12). The control-stage problem is therefore provenance-preserving calibration: cheap self-consistency may inform the record but cannot impersonate external value evidence. (source: futon2 holes labs wm-contract PROBLEMS-assurance-band-batch6.md, R12, The problem it solves)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r12-two-layer-calibration.flexiarg", :sha256 "49eac90f07daa81f9cd6013137eefb2c2681dcd3927b42e7df09fa39dbc7fd2d"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER, dossier R12 provenance-preserving calibration, Layer 1 vs Layer 2.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Calibration evidence here must separate internal consistency (cosine agreement) from externally witnessed value (hand-labeled samples)."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer it; solving the problem itself is scoped by the dossier's residual-problems list, not by this node.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r12-two-layer-calibration.flexiarg", :sha256 "49eac90f07daa81f9cd6013137eefb2c2681dcd3927b42e7df09fa39dbc7fd2d"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER final sentence of the R12 problem statement.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Cheap self-consistency (MiniLM cosine) must not impersonate external value evidence."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [12], :pattern "problems/r12-two-layer-calibration"} {:pattern-rationale "The cross-ref list is the mission reading what exists before acting.", :fragment-span {:start 694, :end 707}, :occurrence-id ["cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first" 13], :roles ["dependency"], :source-sha256 "04b442f40edd33be35382de2355944a0135c50dbefce4a7ec5967378ec21d81e", :sentence-id "s13", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first", :objects {:G {:text "    The disagreements decide which patterns the cascade needs; a cascade built without them restates the requirement.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first.flexiarg", :sha256 "04b442f40edd33be35382de2355944a0135c50dbefce4a7ec5967378ec21d81e"}, :situation-source "Fragment relations [dependency]; pattern THEN 'Read the four sources first and record where they disagree'.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Naming the blocker is recording what exists (the parser's state) first."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A cascade is to be constructed for a problem.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first.flexiarg", :sha256 "04b442f40edd33be35382de2355944a0135c50dbefce4a7ec5967378ec21d81e"}, :situation-source "Fragment 694-707 'Blocks on P-1'.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A blocking dependency (P-1) is declared before any construction."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Reading takes time, and a plausible 