tern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg", :sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"}, :situation-source "Fragment rationale; pattern THEN on known-good/known-bad fixtures and direct probes.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "The sample is the first direct probe of the claimed retrieval property rather than a proxy."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The acceptance signal checks a representation of the property rather than\n    the property itself, especially when imports, definitions, historical\n    state, or human verdicts contribute to the claim.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg", :sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"}, :situation-source "Fragment 1165-1211 'weighting and the first hand-labeled sample.'", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A hand-labeled sample is proposed as the acceptance signal for weighting."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Direct probes can be expensive, and some properties have no complete\n    decision procedure.  A dependency-closure audit may require building\n    previously unbuilt artifacts; a semantic vacuity check remains heuristic.\n    Calling an incomplete probe complete merely creates a new proxy.  State the\n    probe's coverage, retain explicit unknown/skipped outcomes, and reserve\n    acceptance for the portion actually checked.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg", :sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER 'State the probe's coverage, retain explicit unknown/skipped outcomes'.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "One hand-labeled sample is a small, partial probe; its coverage must be stated."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Write the promised property as a checkable question; identify its trust\n    closure; run the strongest available direct probe on every member of that\n    closure; test the probe against known-good, known-bad, and multi-defect\n    fixtures; and make uncovered or skipped members visible non-success states.\n    Keep cheap proxies only as triage filters before this gate.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy.flexiarg", :sha256 "eaa5f4b9e104fea25100f23a959b84682df8ee8e5b153b2c17436f97d3c35c99"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE on gates certifying easier claims when probed by representation.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Cosine agreement would be the proxy; the labeled sample probes the promised property itself."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [22], :pattern "pattern-mining/probe-the-claimed-property-not-the-acceptance-proxy"}], :edges [{:from ["problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale" 0], :to ["problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale" 1], :kind :context-enables, :from-fragment 0, :to-fragment 1, :from-roles ["goal" "context"], :to-roles ["context" "condition"]} {:from ["problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale" 1], :to ["problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale" 2], :kind :condition-enables, :from-fragment 1, :to-fragment 2, :from-roles ["context" "condition"], :to-roles ["context"]} {:from ["problems/most-patterns-have-no-globally-recognised-rationale" 2], :to ["cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first" 3], :kind :context-enables, :from-fragment 2, :to-fragment 3, :from-roles ["context"], :to-roles ["context"]} {:from ["cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first" 3], :to ["problems/llm-over-corpus-mining-lessons" 4], :kind :context-enables, :from-fragment 3, :to-fragment 4, :from-roles ["context"], :to-roles ["context" "dependency"]} {:from ["problems/llm-over-corpus-m